From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thecorporatetractor <marco@azarguard.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:41:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/15] core: add todynamic, replace_regex,
 base64_decode_toarray, column_ifexists

Functions that security queries use and that were missing or broken:
- todynamic(): synonym of parse_json() for strings.
- replace_regex() and the older replace(): .NET regex with Kusto's \0..\9
  back-references in the rewrite pattern; an invalid regex or a timeout (1 s)
  returns the source unchanged.
- base64_decode_toarray(), unicode_codepoints_to_string() and
  unicode_codepoints_from_string(): decode UTF-16 payloads such as
  PowerShell -EncodedCommand.
- column_ifexists(name, default): resolved when the query is translated, as
  in Kusto (the column if the input has it, else the default). It was a stub
  that threw for every input.
- hourofday(): Kusto declares it int; the long implementation never matched
  the signature, so every call failed.
